openOMSI weather preset. OMSI 2 reads it too: it passes the openomsi_preset and
openomsi_sky blocks by. The second number under temp is the dew point (C).

The openomsi_sky block is the sky of openOMSI's Enhanced graphics:
  cumulus cover 0..0.85, grey deck 0..1 (closed from 0.85), cirrus veil (optical depth
  0..2), haze (aerosol against an ordinary clear day: 0.4 crisp .. 3 sultry), its
  Angstrom exponent (1.6 a deep blue sky .. 0.6 a milky one), the hazy layer's depth in
  metres (0 = growing and settling with the day's sun), and (optional) the day's
  exposure in stops (-1.5 the gloom of a storm .. 0 as the eye adapts).

[openomsi_preset]
1

[name]
Between the Showers

[description]
Big showery clouds marching over, blue sky between them, the roads still wet from the last burst.
[end]

